Z||000000||count_iblis||10-22-2000||11:51 PM||||Is the 88' SE rare?  I thought I heard once on here that is was?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||10-23-2000||12:00 AM||||There is no such thing as an '88 SE.  Many people mistakenly call the 4-cyl. coupe an SE, but there really is no '88 SE model (only year not to offer one).  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DjKid||10-23-2000||12:01 AM||||88 didn't have a SE.. it was replaced by the formula..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> so I guess would be, like a 84 with a stock v6  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> or a postal trust that can outrun a fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe - <A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||10-23-2000||12:02 AM||||In 1988 the SE model was dropped and the Formula was introduced. so there are no pre-1988 Fiero Formulas, or anypost-1987 Fiero SEs.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
