Z||000005||count_iblis||10-23-2000||12:12 AM||||Hmmmmmm, there is a guy close buy selling a 88 fiero.  I call him up and ask him if the car he has for sale is an GT?  He says I dont know, let me check the manual and see what it says.  So he comes back to the phone and says that it is a SE?  I guess he just dosent know what year his car is!!!!!!  Anyway im going to call him again and see if i can come out and see it.  This may be wishfull thinking but I just might be a 88 GT!  He said it did have a 6 cyclinder!||||reg||8
Z||000006||Bill H||10-23-2000||04:15 PM|||| Formula are more rare and alittle faster than the GT so mybe it will be a Formula and you live with hand cranking the windows. sorry I'm alittle biased I own a formula. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||10-23-2000||06:38 PM||||There were only about 1500 fewer Formulas built than GT's so they're not much "rarer".<P>You could also order a Formula with power windows and door locks (no power mirrors though), so you don't necessarily need to hand crack those windows.<P>As for this '88 "SE".....it is possible that the quarter windows were replaced with SE ones, so the guy (not knowing any better) calls it an SE.  More common than that though is thinking an '87 is an '88.....this has happened to me more than once!<P>Get the VIN # to clear up any confusion.   ||||reg||10
Z||000008||count_iblis||10-23-2000||10:30 PM||||Hey,<P><BR>Well guys I have cleared this mess out.  The guy went out and double checked the book and low and behold it was a 84 se!  Oh well||||reg||9
Z||000009||mrfiero||10-23-2000||10:46 PM||||What a let down!   All of that and it's just an '84 SE?  Oh well.  If it's really cheap I'd say go ahead and buy it.||||reg||9
